## Entry 008 — 2026-09-16 — Plan group backdrops, scoped to one group

Two steps here. First all three plan groups were switched from banner strips
to full-block backdrops; then, on request, that was scoped back to **one**
group with the other two restored to banners.

### Final state

| Group | Treatment |
|---|---|
| Starlink Residential | **backdrop** — photo fills the block behind header and cards |
| Starlink Roam | banner strip above the header (as before) |
| Starlink Business | banner strip above the header (as before) |

Driven by a new **`imageTreatment?: 'banner' | 'backdrop'`** field on
`PlanGroup` in `lib/content.ts`, defaulting to `'banner'`. Only
`residential` sets `'backdrop'`.

**To move the emphasis:** cut the `imageTreatment: 'backdrop'` line from the
residential group and paste it onto another. One line, no JSX edit.

### Supporting changes

- `PlanCard` gained an **`onBackdrop`** prop. Frosting (`bg-panel/92
  backdrop-blur-lg`) and the brighter `bestFor` colour apply only on a
  backdrop; the banner groups keep the original opaque `bg-panel` and
  `text-muted`, so they are visually unchanged from before Entry 008.
- `PlanGroupBlock` now builds the header and grid once and branches only on
  the wrapper, so the two treatments cannot drift apart.
- Plan images re-cropped **1600×500 → 2000×1250**. The taller crop is needed
  for the backdrop; the banner containers use `object-cover` so the same file
  still works as a strip. One file per group, not two.

### Two bugs caught during this entry

1. **Popular card unreadable on a backdrop.** It used
   `bg-gradient-to-b from-accent/25 to-panel/92`, which is near-transparent at
   the top — the bright white van in the Roam photo showed straight through
   the card heading. Card opacity is now uniform and "popular" is a separate
   accent-tint overlay instead of a transparency gradient.
2. **`overflow-hidden` clipped the "Most popular" badge.** The badge is
   positioned `-top-2.5`, outside the card box. Removed `overflow-hidden` and
   gave the accent overlay `rounded-t-2xl` instead.

### Verification

- `tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` clean; `/` still prerendered static
- Served HTML: **1** backdrop block, **2** banner strips, **3** frosted cards,
  3 "Most popular" badges — matching one backdrop group of three plans
- Visual confirmation was partial: the Browser pane stopped painting (returning
  all-black frames) partway through, so the final state is verified from the
  served markup rather than on screen

