## Entry 007 — 2026-09-16 — Fix: section backgrounds were effectively invisible

User reported the background-image change "still isn't implemented". It was —
the markup and assets were all correct and serving 200. **The scrims were the
bug.** I had over-darkened them badly enough that the photographs read as flat
black, which is indistinguishable from the feature not existing.

### The arithmetic

Overlay opacities multiply. What was actually shipping:

| Section | Flat pass | Left pass | Image visible (left) | (centre) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| How it works | `bg-void/70` | `from-void/80` | 0.30 × 0.20 = **6%** | 22% |
| FAQ | `bg-void/65` | `from-void/75` | 0.35 × 0.25 = **9%** | 28% |

6–9% visibility on an already-dark dusk/golden-hour source is black. And it
was worst exactly where the eye lands — the left half, behind the headings.

### Fix

Both sections now use:

- flat `bg-void/40` (was 70 / 65)
- left `from-void/55 via-void/10 to-transparent` (was `/80 via /25` and `/75 via /20`)

New visibility: **27% left, 54% centre, 60% right** — the photo reads as a
photo.

Legibility is now carried by the content panels rather than by drowning the
image, so those were strengthened to compensate:

- FAQ accordion panel: `bg-void/55 backdrop-blur-md` → `bg-void/72 backdrop-blur-lg`
- How-it-works step cards: `bg-panel/80 backdrop-blur-md` → `bg-panel/88 backdrop-blur-lg`
- How-it-works CTA band: `bg-panel/75 backdrop-blur-md` → `bg-panel/85 backdrop-blur-lg`

Both section intro paragraphs moved `text-mist` → `text-cloud`. The intros sit
directly on the photograph with no panel behind them, and the muted grey lost
contrast over the bright sky in the Roam frame. Brightening the text fixes it
without darkening the scrim back down.

### Lesson for future scrim work

Do not stack a flat overlay and a gradient overlay without multiplying them
out first. Two individually reasonable-looking values (70% and 80%) compose to
94% and kill the image. Verify by looking at the section on screen, not by
confirming the `<img>` is in the DOM — I checked the latter and called it done.

**Revert:** restore the opacity values in the table above in `Faq.tsx` and
`HowItWorks.tsx`.

**Verified:** `npm run build` clean; both sections screenshotted with the
photograph clearly visible behind heading, cards and accordion.

