## Entry 004 — 2026-09-16 — Hero headline + full-bleed FAQ background

### Hero headline

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| High-speed satellite internet, wherever you are. | High-speed satellite internet for homes, vehicles and businesses. |

Names all three product lines the site actually sells (Residential / Roam /
Business) instead of the looser "wherever you are".
**Revert:** `HERO.headline` in `lib/content.ts` — one line.

### FAQ section now has a full-bleed photographic background

The FAQ was the only section on the page with no imagery, sitting between two
image-heavy sections and the footer, so it was the natural place for a
full-bleed backdrop — and it has no card images to compete with.

- New asset **`faq-background.jpg`** (2400×1400), cut from the `og-image`
  original at section proportions. Kept as its own file so it can be swapped
  without disturbing the social preview card.
- `scripts/optimize-images.py` now supports a **source-stem override**, so one
  original can produce several differently-cropped outputs. It also now reads
  from `design/source-images/` rather than `public/images/`.
- Section changed from flat `bg-ink` to `isolate overflow-hidden` with the
  image at `-z-10` and a four-pass scrim:
  - flat `bg-void/65` — overall darkness
  - left-to-right `from-void/75 via-void/20` — keeps the heading rail readable
  - two **fixed-height 28-unit edge bands** (top and bottom) that fade into the
    black sections above and below

  The edge bands are deliberately fixed-height rather than a full-height
  gradient. A first pass used `from-void via-transparent to-void` across the
  whole section, which washed the photograph out almost everywhere except a
  thin middle strip — it read as a dark smudge rather than a background.
- The accordion now sits on a **frosted panel** (`bg-void/55 backdrop-blur-md`,
  rounded, hairline border) so body copy holds contrast wherever the photo is
  brightest, and the section still reads as an enterprise page rather than a
  poster.

**Revert:** in `Faq.tsx`, drop the background `<div>` and the panel classes on
`StaggerGrid`, and restore `bg-ink` on the `<section>`.

### Verification

- `tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` clean; `/` still prerendered static
- `faq-background.jpg` serves 200; optimises to a **127 KB WebP** at 1920w
- 12 `<img>` on the page, 0 broken
- 320px: `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`, zero offending elements — the
  longer headline wraps to 191px tall and does not overflow
- Served image payload: **2.7 MB across 13 files**

