## Entry 002 — 2026-09-16 — Copy, layout and imagery revision

Requested revision pass. Each item below is independently revertable.

### Removed

| What | File | Revert |
|---|---|---|
| Hero background animation (black hole, starfield, parallax, orbital SVG) | `Hero.tsx`; `components/ui/DeepSpace.tsx` **deleted** | Restore `DeepSpace.tsx` from Entry 001 and re-add `<DeepSpace variant="hole" />` + `OrbitalPaths` to `Hero.tsx` |
| Hero "Prefer to talk it through? / Call to order" | `Hero.tsx` | Re-add a `<CallButton>` block after `<ZipChecker />` |
| How-it-works scroll-scrubbed dish assembly (the whole `DishAssembly` SVG, sticky column, `useScroll`/`useSpring`/`useMotionValueEvent` wiring) | `HowItWorks.tsx` — rewritten | Restore the Entry 001 version of the file |

⚠️ **Note:** removing the hero call button reverses the original brief's
"KEEP Hero Call Button" rule. Done on explicit instruction. Phone access is
unaffected — the sticky header CTA sits directly above and stays visible on
scroll, and there are now 19 `tel:` CTAs on the page (up from 17).

### Layout

- Hero top padding `pt-16/sm:pt-24/lg:pt-32` → `pt-10/sm:pt-14/lg:pt-16`,
  and headline `mt-6` → `mt-5`. Closes the gap under the navbar.
- How it works is now a flat 4-up card grid (2-up tablet, 1-up mobile) with a
  photo, step number, title and body per card — the pattern the reference
  retailer sites use. No sticky column, no scroll dependency.
- Hardware cards gained a photo and a **"Call to order"** button pinned to the
  card bottom with `mt-auto` so all three align.

### Copy — all rewritten and moved into `SECTIONS` in `lib/content.ts`

Section headings were previously inline in the JSX. They now live in
`lib/content.ts` under `SECTIONS`, consistent with the rest of the data layer.

| Before | After |
|---|---|
| High-Speed Internet. Anywhere. | High-speed satellite internet, wherever you are. |
| Pick the plan that fits how you connect. | Compare Starlink plans and pricing. |
| Every number, in one place. | Complete plan and pricing comparison. |
| Three kits. One-time cost. | Starlink hardware options. |
| From box to online in about fifteen minutes. | A simple, four-step setup process. |
| Questions worth asking. | Frequently asked questions. |

Also rewritten: hero subline, all three plan-group blurbs, the how-it-works
intro, all four `SETUP_STEPS` titles and bodies, and the how-it-works CTA line.

**All timing claims removed** — the "about fifteen minutes" phrasing is gone
from the how-it-works section *and* from the `faq-install` answer, so the site
makes no install-duration claim anywhere.

*"Frequently asked questions."* was not on the request list, but it was written
in the same voice as the headings that were, so it was changed for consistency.
**Revert:** set `SECTIONS.faq.heading` back to `'Questions worth asking.'`

### Branding — "Northstar Connect LLC" removed everywhere

Zero occurrences remain in `app/`, `components/` or `lib/`.

The footer disclosure could not simply become "Starlink", because
`legalEntity` is interpolated into sentences that would then read *"Starlink is
an independent authorized retailer of Starlink"* — self-referential, and it
would undercut the disclosure that keeps the site from looking like the carrier.
So the disclosures were rephrased to avoid naming an entity at all:

- `retailerDisclosure` → "This site is operated by an independent authorized
  retailer of Starlink. Starlink and the Starlink logo are trademarks of Space
  Exploration Technologies Corp. This site is not operated by Space
  Exploration Technologies Corp."
- `compensation` → "The retailer operating this site receives compensation for
  orders placed through it."
- `legalEntity` / `brandName` → `'Starlink Authorized Retailer'` (used in the
  copyright line and metadata).

**Before launch:** put your real registered company name in `SITE.legalEntity`.
A retailer disclosure naming no legal entity is weaker than one that does.

### Imagery — new `IMAGES` architecture

Image paths live in `lib/content.ts`: the `IMAGES` const, plus an optional
`image?: SiteImage` on `PlanGroup`, `HardwareItem` and each `SETUP_STEPS`
entry. Components render from those, so swapping a photo never touches JSX.

All 12 slots ship with dark on-brand **placeholder JPGs** in `public/images/`
so nothing 404s. Overwrite in place, same filename — no code change needed.
Generator script: `scratchpad/make_placeholders.py`.

Rendering uses `next/image` with `fill` + `sizes`; the hero image carries
`priority` so it is the LCP element and is never lazy-loaded.

Also added: `SITE.siteUrl` + `metadataBase` in `app/layout.tsx`, which clears
the Next build warning and makes OG/Twitter image URLs absolute.

### Verification

- `npm run build` clean, `/` still prerendered static; `tsc --noEmit` clean
- 320px: `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`, zero offending elements
- Hero: `heroHasCallCta: false`, `heroHasZip: true`
- Hardware: 3 cards / 3 CTAs · How it works: 4 cards / 0 animation SVG
- 11 `<img>` elements rendering; 19 `tel:` CTAs all with `data-call-cta`
- Rendered text contains no "fifteen minutes", no "Northstar", no "Prefer to talk"

