### Pricing data — provenance ⚠️ READ THIS

`starlink.com` renders its pricing client-side and blocks automated browsers
(it returned a blank page in both `WebFetch` and a real browser pane), so the
figures below could **not** be read off the official site directly. They were
cross-referenced across four independent trackers that agreed, the most recent
checked 15 Sept 2026:

| Plan | Monthly |
|---|---|
| Residential 100 Mbps | $55 |
| Residential 200 Mbps | $85 |
| Residential Max | $130 |
| Roam 100 GB | $55 |
| Roam 300 GB | $80 |
| Roam Unlimited | $175 |
| Business Priority 50 GB | $55 |
| Business Priority 500 GB | $155 |
| Business Priority 1 TB | $280 |
| Business Priority 2 TB | $530 |

| Hardware | One-time |
|---|---|
| Standard Kit | $349 |
| Starlink Mini | $249 |
| Flat High Performance Kit | $2,500 |

**Action for you:** confirm these against your retailer portal before going
live. Corrections go in `lib/content.ts` and nowhere else.

Two earlier sources disagreed and were **rejected** as stale: one still listed
a retired "Residential Lite" tier, another quoted a $599 Roam kit. Starlink
restructured Residential from named tiers to speed tiers; "Residential Lite"
no longer exists in the US.

### Placeholder identity — replace before launch

In `lib/content.ts` → `SITE`:
`brandName`, `legalEntity`, `phoneDisplay`, `phoneHref`, `hours`, `address`,
`email`. All are invented placeholders. Changing `phoneHref` updates all 17
`tel:` links at once.

`LEGAL_LINKS` points at `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/disclaimer`, `/tcpa`,
`/cookies` — **these routes do not exist yet** and will 404.

### Negative constraints — all honoured

- ✅ No support-routing copy anywhere
- ✅ Hero keeps **both** ZIP checker and call button
- ✅ Body CTAs say only "Call to order" / "Call for pricing" — never the raw
  number. Header and footer show the number, as specified.
- ✅ No competitor bashing; no "ordering channel, not the network operator"
- ✅ No fiber / cable / bundle / TV / mobile / phone sections. Enforced
  structurally: `getActiveServiceLines()` filters out lines with zero plans,
  so they cannot render even as empty placeholders.
- ✅ No Broadband Facts label link
- ✅ No "Pricing observed [date]" stamp
- ✅ No "Is this the official site?" FAQ

### Verification performed

- `npm run build` — clean; `/` prerendered as static content
- `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean
- **Horizontal overflow at 320px:** `scrollWidth === clientWidth === 320`,
  zero offending elements
- **`data-call-cta`:** 17 of 17 `tel:` links carry it
- **Body CTA labels:** only `["Call to order"]`; zero raw phone numbers
- **Banned strings:** all six checked against rendered text — none present
- **No hard-coded data in layout files:** grep for dollar amounts, plan names,
  speeds, phone numbers and CTA strings across `app/` + `components/` returns
  nothing but explanatory comments
- **Live propagation test:** changed `residential-100` price to a sentinel in
  `lib/content.ts` → it appeared in **6** render sites (hero lockup + its
  sr-only string, plan card + its sr-only string, desktop table row, mobile
  card). Reverted afterwards.

---

### Bugs found and fixed during the build

Recording these because each was subtle and could plausibly reappear.

1. **Tailwind utilities silently overridden by unlayered CSS**
   `globals.css` had base resets written outside any cascade layer. Unlayered
   CSS outranks *every* `@layer`, so `a { color: inherit }` beat Tailwind's
   `text-void` and the header call button rendered white-on-white.
   *Fix:* base resets moved into `@layer base`, custom classes into
   `@layer components`. **Keep new element-level CSS inside `@layer base`.**

2. **`whileInView` could never fire on masked words**
   `RevealText` put the in-view trigger on each word span, but each word
   starts translated 105% down — fully outside its own `overflow-hidden`
   mask. IntersectionObserver clips against overflowing ancestors, so the
   intersection rect was always empty and the words hid themselves forever.
   *Fix:* trigger moved to the unclipped heading; words animate via variant
   propagation. **Never attach `whileInView` to an element that starts
   outside its own clip.**

3. **SVG `d` attribute morphing**
   The hamburger animated `d` between paths with different command
   structures; motion can't interpolate those and emitted `d="undefined"`.
   *Fix:* three bars on the centre line, spread with `translateY`, animated
   with transforms only.

4. **`transform-origin` is not a React DOM property**
   Used as a JSX attribute in `HowItWorks.tsx`. *Fix:* moved into `style` as
   `transformOrigin`.

5. **Conditional hook call** — `useTransform` was called inside JSX in
   `TiltCard.tsx`, breaking the Rules of Hooks. *Fix:* hoisted to top level.

6. **JSX comment as a second child** — a `{/* */}` comment placed beside an
   element inside `{cond && ( … )}` is a parse error. *Fix:* comment moved
   above the conditional.

7. **320px header overflow** — logo + full phone number + menu button summed
   past 320px, and `overflow-x: hidden` would have clipped the menu button
   out of reach. *Fix:* added `--breakpoint-xs: 25rem`; below it the header
   shows the orbital mark alone (`<Logo compact />`). The footer keeps the
   full lockup. **Revert:** drop `compact` from `Logo` in `Header.tsx`.

8. **Motion overrides SVG `transformOrigin`** — motion normalises SVG
   transforms to `transform-box: fill-box` with a `50% 50%` origin, so the
   explicit pixel origins set on the dish, satellite and mast were silently
   discarded. Centre origin is correct for the dish and satellite, so those
   dead props were removed; the mast now uses `originY: 1` (a value motion
   does honour) so it telescopes up out of the base instead of expanding
   from its middle. **Revert:** remove `originY: 1` from the mast's `style`
   in `HowItWorks.tsx`.

---

### Known gaps (deliberate — frontend-only build)

- ZIP checker does no real lookup. It validates format, then directs to a
  call. There is no backend by design.
- Legal routes are linked but not built.
- No `opengraph-image`; the default Next favicon is still in place.
